CONCEPT
  product : Duos.
  one-liner: Custody weekends, restructured as a competitive live-service season.
  The bit: a live-service games company has decided standard visitation is a game mode. The court
  order is the ruleset, the driveway is the extraction point, the kid is a squadmate. Storm circle
  closes on Sunday 6:00 PM. 100-tier season pass with no Tier 100. Emote wheel replaces free text
  with the co-parent at every price point including the $1,400 one.
  anti-ai-slop invoked before all copy (steps 2, 5, 6). Zero em dashes across concept, landing and
  demo. No throat-clearing, no corrective antithesis, no gift-wrapped closers.

DESIGN DIRECTION
  style   : Extruded clay game-launcher, season-announcement daylight mode
  palette : primary #2F55E8 cobalt (sole carrier) / accent #FF2E74 custody magenta (quarantined to
            schedule telemetry only) / bg #E9EDFB periwinkle / fg #1A1F33 / muted #6B7391 / ink #131728
  fonts   : Fredoka (display) + Nunito Sans (body) + Spline Sans Mono (telemetry figures)
  archetype: live-service game season page
  ANTI-SAMENESS CHECK vs last 7 entries (09-03 aurora glass console, 09-02 supergraphic identity
  manual, 09-01 automotive press configurator, 08-31 glossy magazine editorial, 08-30 diazo drawing
  set, 08-29 totalisator board, 08-28 monochrome bento lattice): no collision on style, palette or
  font pair. Clay volume was explicitly banned by five of the last seven, so this is a clean break.
  Fredoka, Nunito Sans and Spline Sans Mono are all first uses in the run history.

IMAGES  (4 generated, 5 API calls, 1 regeneration)
  rationale: style archetype is clay, so every slot is a soft 3D clay-render, never photography.
    - hero      : taken, but as a 1:1 clay avatar seated inside the hero storm ring instead of a
                  16:9 landscape plate. A wide photographic band would have fought the tile stack.
    - demo      : no separate generation. The pre-drop lobby's only photo-shaped slots are the
                  avatar plate and the squad rail, both of which reuse hero.webp so the same man
                  appears in the pitch and in his own lobby.
    - testimonials: all three named users given clay headshots. Remaining budget went here.
  per-image:
    hero.webp    640x640  13.9 KB  attempts 1  PASS — correct subject, cobalt polo and magenta
                 wristband carry the palette discipline, rolled mat lands the air-mattress bit,
                 flat deadpan expression, clean periwinkle seamless, no text artifacts.
    shot-1.webp  320x320   7.0 KB  attempts 1  PASS — HVAC-manager read is exact, blue work shirt
                 holds the palette. Slightly more sculpted realism than the hero; kept, because the
                 variance reads as different players rather than as a different renderer.
    shot-2.webp  320x320   6.1 KB  attempts 1  PASS — whistle lanyard sells the rec-soccer
                 credential with no text, glasses and shaved head differentiate him cleanly.
    shot-3.webp  320x320   7.4 KB  attempts 2  attempt 1 FAILED the palette-harmony check: returned
                 an unpainted warm terracotta bust with a realistic pained sculpt, the only warm
                 image on a cool page and reading as a different medium from the other three.
                 Regenerated once with explicit corrective feedback on colour, value and facial
                 simplification. Attempt 2 PASS: cobalt sweatshirt, magenta earcups carrying the
                 rationed accent, smooth toy-like face, calm expression, cool light values.
  All four judged with vision via Read. All well under the 500 KB cap. No image dropped.
  GEMINI_API_KEY present, no cap hit.

BUILD
  landing : frontend-design invoked. Clay slabs on periwinkle, hero split between a monumental
            Fredoka claim and a CSS storm ring holding the avatar, live countdown to the next
            Sunday 6:00 PM extraction in magenta mono, four-cell telemetry strip, three feature
            slabs with tier-node indices, three testimonial slabs with clay-ringed headshots,
            three pricing slabs with the middle edition flooded cobalt, closing slab, footer.
  demo    : pre-drop lobby as a game launcher. Squad rail (you READY / squadmate EN ROUTE ETA
            6:14 PM), live storm timer, three tabs (Lobby / Season pass / Loadout), a CSS-built
            one-bedroom apartment stage with the avatar standing in it, a scrollable tier rail
            where 62 is claimable and everything past it is locked with a stated reason, a
            rarity-filtered loadout grid with expandable item detail, and a modal emote wheel of
            eight driveway gestures with six locked behind the paid edition. Vanilla JS only,
            no frameworks, no network calls. Escape and scrim-click close the modal, focus is
            returned to the trigger, prefers-reduced-motion respected on both pages.

