VISUAL CHECK (step 9, run: playwright already present, ~27 tool calls at entry)
  2 captures taken, 2 corrective edits, 1 re-capture. Under every cap.
  landing: no breakage. No overlap, no off-canvas element, images at correct aspect, contrast holds.
  demo: two real defects found and fixed.
    1. The lobby avatar rendered 212px wide by 640px tall. .avatar set width but never height:auto,
       so the img element's height="640" presentational hint won and stretched the figure the full
       length of the stage. Fixed with height:auto.
    2. The empty toast rendered as a stray black pill at the page bottom in full-page capture.
       translateY(140%) alone did not hide it. Fixed with opacity:0 / pointer-events:none until .show.
  Re-capture confirms both fixed and nothing else regressed. No taste-level tweaks made.

